# Android Studio auto-generates local.properties with your sdk.dir when you
# first open this project - do NOT delete that line.
#
# Add this line yourself, underneath the sdk.dir line, using your own key:
#
# GOOGLE_TASKS_API_KEY=AIzaSyDr9EfxaecVp3zliYkFtg5jvnO1Fkfylxo
#
# This file (local.properties.example) is just a template committed to the
# project so teammates know what to add. The real local.properties file is
# in .gitignore and never gets committed, which is exactly where an API key
# should live - never hardcoded directly in a .kt file or build.gradle.
